00:15.760 --> 00:16.920
16.

00:16.920 --> 00:22.520
I personally think that you all did a very credible job in helping the science support room

00:22.520 --> 00:31.320
and pre-flighting to get all the experiments ready to prepare the crew and the flight for Apollo 16.

00:31.320 --> 00:36.560
I think that looking back at it now, we can say we had a very successful mission that

00:36.560 --> 00:39.480
we attained tremendous amount of information from the flight.

00:39.480 --> 00:44.600
I know that the rock boxes back there at the curatorial facility are bursting at their

00:44.600 --> 00:48.480
