39:54.800 --> 40:01.800
The main difference between the foil of Apollo 16 and the ones of the previous missions

40:01.800 --> 40:08.800
is that some pieces of platinum foil have been attached to the previous design,

40:08.800 --> 40:12.800
which was composed of a pure aluminum foil.

40:12.800 --> 40:17.800
This platinum foil piece can be cleaned by a floridic acid,

40:17.800 --> 40:23.800
which allows to remove all the possible lunar dust contamination.

40:23.800 --> 40:28.800
This technique has been tested in the lab on bombarded foils

40:28.800 --> 40:34.800
and showed that you can remove essentially all the lunar dust contamination

40:34.800 --> 40:41.800
without losing any measurable amount of trapped rare gas ions,

40:41.800 --> 40:45.800
or atoms of solar wind origin.

40:45.800 --> 40:57.800
This technique should allow us to determine the isotopic composition of the rare gas elements of solar wind origin

40:57.800 --> 41:03.800
up to the mass of possibly Krypton.

